{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>You have sown</b> — and what comes — grain into the house, little." "<b>Eat</b> — you [plural] eat." "<b>For drunkenness</b> — like לשבעה. In the manner of 'you eat and are not satisfied,' for there are times when people eat much and are not satisfied, and likewise one drinks much and there is no drunkenness — not that the nature [of drink] has changed to intoxicate. And know that the word חם is difficult, for behold it is written: 'My heart was חם within me' — and this is the truth — and 'it was חם to them' requires that the air be heating and thusly, and there is no heating to it. And חום, in the pattern of קור, is of the doubled-letter forms [פעלי הכפל], and this is its interpretation from his mouth. And if it is from חמם, the vocalization proves it, for all doubled-letter forms, when the letter of doubling is removed, are vocalized with pataḥ — like 'if the silver is תם,' which is תמם. And we cannot say that it is like שב, for sometimes it is an intransitive verb — he returns himself — and sometimes a transitive verb, like 'and He will restore your fortunes' (ושב את שבותך), for ושב has kamatz and חם has pataḥ." "<b>Purse</b> — like 'a purse of silver' (צרור הכסף). And if it were pierced, nothing would be found in it."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "The phrase ואין לחום לו is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The identity of 'his mouth' (מפיו) is uncertain — possibly referring to a named grammarian source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:27.892314048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}